<main><h1>Anees Engine Report</h1>
<p class="lead">Every speech-to-text engine tried for the Palestinian Arabic lessons, all on the same Aug 25 recording (62 min, Medi + Amal, Arabic and English mixed). Written 2026-09-04.</p>
<div class="verdict">Verdict: ElevenLabs Scribe v2 is the engine for now. It won Amal's blind vote 15 of 20 against Speechmatics and the local engine (ChatGPT was not in that vote), keeps the most hesitations, labels speakers, and costs $0.22 per hour. Against ChatGPT it wins on words kept and speaker labels, not on a human accuracy score: nobody has written a word-perfect transcript yet.</div>
<div class="verdict" style="border-left-color:var(--amber)">Codex independent test (same day, 2026-09-04, new lesson, pre-registered): ElevenLabs kept 725 tokens and 22 fillers on 20 clips; ChatGPT's strict prompt kept 590 tokens and 0 fillers; feeding it the vocab list made it slightly worse. Full report: <a href="https://github.com/TheNatanzi/anees/blob/master/wiki/16-codex-independent-test-2026-09-04.md">wiki/16</a>.</div>
